# ofxManifold serialization conformance vectors
# GENERATED by tests/ref/reference_serialize.py -- do not hand edit
#
# The C++ parses these fixtures with the hand-written parser in
# src/io; this reference parses the same files with Python's
# json module. That is an independent implementation of the
# format written by neither of us, which makes agreement here
# the strongest cross-check in the project.

TOL 1e-06

# a plain three-node manifold
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_simple ANALYTIC simple.json OK
COUNTS counts_simple ANALYTIC simple.json 3 1
EVAL eval_centroid CROSS simple.json 0.48333333 0.43333333 A=0.3333333417 B=0.3333333298 C=0.3333333285
EVAL eval_interior CROSS simple.json 0.45 0.4 A=0.417218543 B=0.298013245 C=0.2847682119
ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_simple ANALYTIC simple.json

# per-node weights must survive the file. A loader that
# dropped them would still produce a valid-looking manifold
# and every weight would be quietly wrong.
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_biased ANALYTIC biased.json OK
EVAL eval_biased CROSS biased.json 0.45 0.4 A=0.6545454545 B=0.2337662338 C=0.1116883117
ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_biased ANALYTIC biased.json

# absent weight defaults to 1, and absent "space" is
# accepted, so a hand-written file stays short
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_no_weights ANALYTIC no_weights.json OK
EVAL eval_no_weights CROSS no_weights.json 0.45 0.4 A=0.417218543 B=0.298013245 C=0.2847682119

# four regions: region order must survive, since first-hit
# containment depends on it
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_fan ANALYTIC fan.json OK
COUNTS counts_fan ANALYTIC fan.json 5 4
EVAL eval_fan_q0 CROSS fan.json 0.62 0.62 O=0.4 N=0.3 E=0.3
EVAL eval_fan_q2 CROSS fan.json 0.38 0.38 O=0.4 S=0.3 W=0.3
ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_fan ANALYTIC fan.json

# positions chosen so that six significant digits LOSE the
# float and nine keep it. Every other fixture here uses short
# decimals such as 0.2 and 0.85, which survive six digits by
# accident -- so the write precision was untested until this
# fixture existed. See DECISIONS.md D-007.
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_precision ANALYTIC precision.json OK
ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_precision ANALYTIC precision.json

# escaped quotes and backslashes in node names. The writer
# quotes names on the way out, so a parser and a writer that
# disagree about escaping produce a file that will not reload.
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_escapes ANALYTIC escapes.json OK
COUNTS counts_escapes ANALYTIC escapes.json 3 1
ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_escapes ANALYTIC escapes.json

# exponent notation in several forms. A hand-rolled number
# parser that stopped at the decimal point would read 1e-3 as
# 1 and place the node in the wrong place entirely.
MANIFOLD_LOAD load_exponents ANALYTIC exponents.json OK
EVAL eval_exponents CROSS exponents.json 0.45 0.4 A=0.2389350324 B=0.4597792695 C=0.301285698

# files that must be REFUSED. A loader that accepts these
# hands back a manifold that is wrong rather than absent,
# which is worse than failing.
#
# Each rejection also asserts a SUBSTRING of the error. That is
# not decoration: a loader can refuse a file for the right
# verdict and the wrong reason, and the person reading the
# message at six in the evening is the one who pays. Checking
# only accept/reject let a mutation through that dropped the
# dangling-node check entirely -- the file was still refused,
# by a later guard, with a message naming the wrong problem.
# Substrings are OUR message text, hence SPEC where they are
# the only thing under test.
# trailing comma is not JSON
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_trailing_comma ANALYTIC bad_trailing_comma.json FAIL expected
# truncated file
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_unterminated ANALYTIC bad_unterminated.json FAIL unexpected_end
# a file with no version cannot be interpreted safely
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_no_version ANALYTIC bad_no_version.json FAIL missing_version
# a future version is refused rather than read as best it can be
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_future_version ANALYTIC bad_future_version.json FAIL unsupported_version
# an unknown space is refused rather than assumed normalized -- reading pixel coordinates as normalized would put every node within a fraction of the origin and look like a collapsed map
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_unknown_space SPEC bad_unknown_space.json FAIL unsupported_space
# duplicate keys are an error, not last-wins. Note the duplicate is "triangles" and both values are VALID -- a last-wins parser would load this file happily. An earlier version of this fixture duplicated "version" with values 1 and 2, which a last-wins parser also rejected, as an unsupported version. It passed on a coincidence and tested nothing (D-007)
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_duplicate_key SPEC bad_duplicate_key.json FAIL duplicate_key
# two nodes with the same id
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_duplicate_node ANALYTIC bad_duplicate_node.json FAIL duplicate_node_id
# a triangle naming a node that does not exist
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_dangling_triangle ANALYTIC bad_dangling_triangle.json FAIL unknown_node
# collinear vertices: refused at load, not discovered at evaluate
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_degenerate_triangle ANALYTIC bad_degenerate_triangle.json FAIL degenerate
# a position with one component
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_short_position ANALYTIC bad_short_position.json FAIL position
# content after the closing brace
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_trailing_junk ANALYTIC bad_trailing_junk.json FAIL trailing_content
# the root is not an object
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_root_array ANALYTIC bad_root_array.json FAIL not_an_object
# an unterminated string as the ROOT value. This is the only place the fault is observable: anywhere inside an object or array, the enclosing container fails first and hides it. With no container, a parser that returned the partial string would report 'root is not an object' instead, which is the wrong diagnosis for the file
MANIFOLD_LOAD reject_unterminated_string ANALYTIC bad_unterminated_string.json FAIL unterminated

# a mapping loaded against simple.json. Bindings refer to
# nodes BY NAME: NodeIDs are runtime handles whose values
# depend on insertion order, and writing them to disk would
# make the file silently wrong the moment someone reorders
# the nodes in their manifold.
MAPPING_LOAD load_mapping ANALYTIC simple.json mapping_simple.json OK
MAPPING_TARGETS mapping_targets ANALYTIC simple.json mapping_simple.json 4
# Target NAMES, not just how many. Counting alone cannot see a
# writer that emits numeric ids instead of names: the file
# reloads into four targets called "0" through "3", the count
# matches, byte stability holds, and every OSC address in the
# show is wrong.
MAPPING_NAMES mapping_names ANALYTIC simple.json mapping_simple.json out.1 out.2 corner.NW corner.NE
MAPPING_ROUNDTRIP roundtrip_mapping ANALYTIC simple.json mapping_simple.json

# a binding naming a node the manifold does not have. A mapping is only meaningful against a manifold, so this is a load failure rather than a warning
MAPPING_LOAD reject_dangling SPEC simple.json bad_map_dangling.json FAIL unknown_node
# an aggregator mode that does not exist
MAPPING_LOAD reject_mode ANALYTIC simple.json bad_map_mode.json FAIL unknown_aggregator_mode
# no version
MAPPING_LOAD reject_no_version ANALYTIC simple.json bad_map_no_version.json FAIL version
